  "notes": "{意図|いと} refers to a deliberate, calculated intention behind an action. It often implies a planned or strategic purpose.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {意図|いと}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to intend, to aim for\n- {意図|いと}⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{読|よ}めない→読む：00426_yomu⟧: can't read the intention\n- {意図|いと}⟦した→する：00392_suru⟧⟦{通|とお}り→通り：01475_toori⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧: as intended\n- {意図|いと}せず: unintentionally\n- {意図|いと}{的|てき}⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧: intentionally, deliberately\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {意図|いと}: intention, aim (deliberate, calculated, may imply hidden motive)\n- ⟦{意向|いこう}→意向：12624_ikou⟧: intention, wishes (formal wishes regarding decisions)\n- ⟦{目的|もくてき}→目的：02433_mokuteki⟧: purpose, objective (the goal itself)\n- ⟦{狙|ねら}い→狙い：00312_nerai⟧: aim, target (what one is aiming for, slightly informal)",
